========================================================================
  THE GENERATING FUNCTION NEAR x=4
========================================================================

  F(x) = Σ (1 + R(n)) x^n = 1/(1-x) + G(x)
  where G(x) ≈ x³/(2(1-x/4)^4) for the 3-cycle correction.
  Poles: x=1 (from identity), x=4 (from 3-cycle correction).

  The RADIUS 4 = 2² comes from 2^{2n} in the Delta_3 exponent.
  For k=5: pole at x = 2^4 = 16.
  For k=7: pole at x = 2^6 = 64.
  General k: pole at x = 2^{k-1}.

  The poles form a GEOMETRIC SEQUENCE: 4, 16, 64, 256, ...
  = 4^1, 4^2, 4^3, 4^4, ...
  No wait: 2^{k-1} for k=3,5,7,9 = 4, 16, 64, 256.
  Ratios: 4, 4, 4, ... YES: poles at 4^{(k-1)/2} for odd k.
  = 4, 4², 4³, 4⁴ for k=3,5,7,9.

